    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d205">

                <pb facs="0247" n="157" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg157"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1736</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Reinsch</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-05-08T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 8, 1918, 4
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your May 4, 5 p.m.,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d205-f1"/> and April 25, 5 p.m.<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d205-f2"/> The Department’s telegrams of May 1, 5 p.m., May 4,
                    4 p.m., and May 6, 5 p.m.,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d205-f3"/> state clearly the
                    attitude of this Government towards contending factions in Russia. Strict
                    neutrality is desirable and must be observed. Although Allied governments have
                    not recognized the Soviet they are interested in stimulating its opposition to
                    the Central powers. No Allied commission for organizing representative or other
                    government in Siberia is deemed advisable.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d205-f1" n="1" xml:id="d205-f1-content">
                <p>This telegram read: “Please reply my telegram Apr. 25, 5 p.m.”</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d205-f2" n="2" xml:id="d205-f2-content">
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg137">p. 137</ref>.</p>
